          "message": {
            "text": "Fresh-process isolation is part of the parity contract. A shared renderer/browser lifecycle stalled when the corpus reached the iframe after earlier composed pages, while one child process per fixture completed all seven rows in 11.3 seconds; tests/composed-parity-corpus.e2e.test.ts keeps the intentional in-page mutation transitions explicit, so isolation removes cross-case state without weakening any comparison. The hard three-platform consumer is .github/workflows/composed-parity-corpus.yml.",
            "markdown": "Fresh-process isolation is part of the parity contract. A shared renderer/browser lifecycle stalled when the corpus reached the iframe after earlier composed pages, while one child process per fixture completed all seven rows in 11.3 seconds; tests/composed-parity-corpus.e2e.test.ts keeps the intentional in-page mutation transitions explicit, so isolation removes cross-case state without weakening any comparison. The hard three-platform consumer is .github/workflows/composed-parity-corpus.yml."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/run-composed-parity.mjs"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 14,
                  "endLine": 31,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  // A fresh process per composed page is intentional. The corpus crosses\n  // global font/image/gradient caches, iframe recursion, and replaced-surface\n  // ownership; sharing one renderer session would turn its order into an\n  // unrecorded eighth axis and has already exposed a post-gradient iframe\n  // stall. The separate live E2E test owns deliberate state transitions.\n  writeFileSync(resultPath, \"\", \"utf8\");\n  const child = spawnSync(\n    process.execPath,\n    [\"--import\", \"tsx\", \"tests/composed-parity.ts\", \"--only\", fixture.name, \"--workers\", \"1\"],\n    { cwd: root, env: process.env, stdio: \"inherit\" },\n  );\n  if (child.error != null) {\n    console.error(`Unable to run ${fixture.name}: ${child.error.message}`);\n    failed = true;\n    continue;\n  }\n  if (child.status !== 0) failed = true;\n  try {"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
